 "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Hawaii sits among the most Democratic states in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly 13 points toward Democrats and a decades-long record of supporting Democratic nominees. The Republican incumbent is term-limited, so both sides enter an open race with no incumbency advantage for either party.\n\nNo public general-election polls, expert ratings, or candidate fundraising figures are available for this contest. The forecast therefore rests on the state's fundamentals, which point to a comfortable but not insurmountable Democratic advantage. Hawaii's electorate did shift noticeably rightward in the last presidential cycle, a reminder that margins here can move with the national climate even as the overall direction of the state remains firmly Democratic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9253, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8703, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9295, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8784, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.877, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8862, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.878, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8719, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8743, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8792, "margin": 13.0}]}